---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TitleComponent from "../components/misc/TitleComponent.astro";
import SeparatorComponent from "../components/misc/SeparatorComponent.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <TitleComponent Titulo="Terms of Service" />
    <SeparatorComponent />
    <main class="pb-20 px-5 font-jost mx-10">

        <p class="mb-6">
            Welcome to the SpaceX Store website, (the "Site"). The Site is provided as a service to our fans and customers. Please review the following terms and conditions of use, including an Arbitration Agreement, which govern your use of the Site (the "Agreement").
        </p>
        <p class="mb-6 font-bold">
            YOUR USE OF THE SITE CONSTITUTES YOUR AGREEMENT TO FOLLOW AND BE BOUND BY THE AGREEMENT. WE RESERVE THE RIGHT TO UPDATE OR MODIFY THIS AGREEMENT AT ANY TIME WITHOUT PRIOR NOTICE. FOR THIS REASON, WE ENCOURAGE YOU TO REVIEW THE AGREEMENT WHENEVER YOU USE ANY OF THE SITE. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO THESE TERMS, PLEASE DO NOT USE THE SITE.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Site Transactions</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            We reserve the right to refuse any order you place with us. We may limit or cancel quantities purchased per person, household, or order, including orders under the same account, credit card, or address. In the event we change or cancel an order, we will attempt to notify you. We may limit or prohibit orders appearing to be placed by dealers or resellers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Right to Change Site</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            We may modify, suspend, or discontinue the Site or any feature, with or without notice. We may charge or waive fees at our discretion. We are not liable for any modification, suspension, or discontinuance.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Site Contents</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            Unless otherwise noted, all materials on the Site, including text, images, icons, video clips, and other content, are owned, controlled, or licensed by SpaceX. Trademarks appearing on the Site are the property of SpaceX and its subsidiaries.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">User Comments, Feedback, and Other Submissions</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            SpaceX welcomes comments but cannot accept unsolicited creative ideas. By submitting comments, you allow SpaceX to use, edit, copy, publish, and distribute them. You are responsible for your comments and must not violate third-party rights or submit unlawful material.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Personal Information Submitted Through the Site</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            Submission of personal information is governed by our Privacy Policy, incorporated by reference into this Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Errors, Inaccuracies, and Omissions</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            We may correct errors or omissions, including product descriptions, pricing, and availability, at any time without prior notice.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Colors & Style</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            We strive to display accurate product colors and styles but cannot guarantee monitor displays are exact.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Indemnification</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            You agree to defend and hold SpaceX harmless from any claims, damages, costs, and expenses arising from your use of the Site or breach of the Agreement.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium mt-8 mb-4">Dispute Resolution and Arbitration Agreement</h2>
        <h3 class="font-medium">Informal Dispute Resolution</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
            Both you and SpaceX agree to try to resolve disputes in good faith by written notice and a 30-day response period prior to arbitration or court action.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-medium">Arbitration Agreement</h3>
        <p class="mb-6">
            Disputes unresolved informally will be handled through binding arbitration via the American Arbitration Association (AAA). This includes waiving rights to class actions or jury trials. Arbitration is individual and governed by the AAA Rules and the Federal Arbitration Act.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">Termination</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            Except for the Arbitration Agreement, these terms remain effective until terminated by you or SpaceX. SpaceX may deny access if you fail to comply. Obligations incurred prior to termination survive.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-medium">General</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
            These terms are governed by California law, except arbitration which is governed by the Federal Arbitration Act. If any provision is unenforceable, remaining provisions remain in effect. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement regarding Site use.
        </p>
    </main>
</Layout>